        "rootCause": "Two interacting issues cause this false positive: (1) Ordinary Spanish function and polite words (`las` +3.32, `favor` +2.05, `con` +1.73, `por` +1.50, `sus` +0.44, `lista` +0.32) have strong positive weights in `MODEL_FEATURES` because Spanish tokens in the public Enron/SpamAssassin training corpora appear almost exclusively in spam while all 100 synthetic clinical TRAIN rows (`harness/evaluation/clinical-train.json`) are English-only; those 5 everyday Spanish words alone satisfy `>= 5` positive body words and exceed the `4.59511985` logit cutoff (`margin = 6.186`). (2) `normalizeText` uses `NFKC` (preserving precomposed Latin diacritics such as `ñ`, `í`, `é`, `ó`) while `statisticalTokens` and `contextFeatures` extract `/[a-z]+/g`, splitting accented Latin words mid-token (`mañana` -> `ana`, `clínica` -> `nica`, `médico` -> `dico`) into spurious positive-weight substrings."
      }
    }
